    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0413" n="1167" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.5411/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-07T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 8, 8.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1012. The Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me that a special mission will
                    accompany Minister Sulzer to the United States in order <pb facs="0414" n="1168"
                        xml:id="pg1168"/> to explain the peculiar economic conditions of Switzerland
                    in connection with the possible restriction of foodstuff shipments from America.
                    It will be composed of Federal Councilor Syz, president of the Swiss Chamber of
                    Commerce; William Rappard, professor of political economy in Genera and exchange
                    professor of Harvard University; and Lieutenant Colonel Staempfli of Berne,
                    president of the Central Committee for the Occupation of Internes.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
